                        "entry_id": "56ee807c-fcf9-32fa-abac-4079bf5d7ec3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In the Levant, a small coffee cup without a handle, held instead in a zarf."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a62f7098-b1c1-4b1c-ac93-7a68c75f09f5",
                                "sense_id": "e19d1285-82c2-3c52-b1df-0a7efca90587",
                                "text": "On each side is a tray, covered with a snoy napkin, the edges worked with gold and silver flowers, upon one are handsome finjans in filigree, silver coffee-cups, and sugar-basins; on the other, cut-glass saucers full of delicious candied sweetmeats, of which the orange- flower, violet and rose are the most fragrant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9c9a887-9a5a-42a3-bc31-e5fb3e1a85da",
                                "sense_id": "e19d1285-82c2-3c52-b1df-0a7efca90587",
                                "text": "Luis spooned Turkish coffee and sugar into a finjan and, after lighting the stoves in an accomplished manner, he cooked the eggs and boiled the coffee three times."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d0a10d1-2d05-4fa5-995a-b4cbe37c5a1e",
                                "sense_id": "e19d1285-82c2-3c52-b1df-0a7efca90587",
                                "text": "The coffee-shops were already crowded with lean and hungry customers, the pipes were filled and lighted, and the coffee smoked in the finjans."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
